message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Evaluating LLM-Based Credit Rating Systems: A Pre-Registered Specification-Curve Analysis — reproducibility artifact"
abstract: >
  Reproducibility artifact (code, frozen response corpus, analysis outputs) for a
  pre-registered specification-curve study of LLM credit-rating instability. From a frozen
  90-item battery x 32 specifications x 3 seeds (~8,640 elicitations, two providers)
  the analysis regenerates the variance decomposition, determinism-subgrid permutation test,
  within/cross-vendor agreement, granularity-kappa, and the economic translation (turnover,
  Cornaggia-anchored spread, post-hoc Basel capital recast, RCAP calibration). A decontaminated
  real-firm arm (31 anonymized, perturbed issuers benchmarked to disclosed agency ratings; a
  pre-registered fingerprinting gate) shows the WATCH-stratum flip-share replicates (not
  distinguishable from the constructed battery; a formal TOST equivalence test is inconclusive
  at this sample size). A post-hoc flagship model-tier arm (gpt-5.4 + gemini-3.1-pro-preview on the
  frozen 12-specification grid, 1,620 elicitations) finds no evidence that the instability attenuates
  on larger models. The artifact also derives and validates a deployable specification-instability
  score (ROC-AUC 0.94 on held-out specifications; 0.70 on the real-issuer arm) with a self-consistency
  curve and per-issuer cost model. Repository: https://github.com/samirrc2/llm-credit-rating-specification-curve
type: software
